STEER-F: produce the future-entropy forecast and turn it into A_H.

  dp_actor.py       one extra no-grad forward per micro-batch with
                    output_hidden_states=True -> H_togo; compute_log_prob now
                    returns 4 values.
  fsdp_workers.py   unpack the 4th value and ship "h_togo" in the DataProto.
                    (This also fixes an upstream latent bug: line ~772 already
                    unpacked 4 values from the 3-tuple, so any run with a
                    standalone reference policy -- use_kl_loss=True or
                    use_kl_in_reward=True -- crashed before this patch.)
  ray_trainer.py    build A_H with the sibling baseline, which needs the whole
                    prompt group and therefore cannot live in the actor.

SCOPE NOTE: unlike the other patches in this directory, this one could not be
executed during development -- it needs a GPU, and the environment it was
written in has none. The logic it calls is unit-tested (tests/), but the FSDP
parameter-gathering path in _steerf_unembedding() is untested. Read the
docstring there before the first multi-GPU run.

